Final Checklist
- The letter must be signed. Witnessing or notarization is not required.
- Send the original signed letter to the U.S. Department of State.
- Submit copies of supporting documents unless an original is specifically required.
- Include the original copy of Form DS-64 (Statement Regarding Lost or Stolen Passport).
- Retain a complete copy of the letter and all enclosures for your records.
- Use a trackable delivery method and follow up after a reasonable period.

